                <pb facs="1118" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg998"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-05T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your 15, April 29, 11 A.M.</p>
                <p>If the corporation desires further representations, you will earnestly impress
                    upon the President that Department would view with concern any action by the
                    Costa Rican Government looking to the arbitrary cancellation of the contract or
                    disregarding the provisions of Article 14 for the arbitration of disputes
                    between the Government and the contractor. You will urge that this Government
                    expects the American interests concerned to receive from the Costa Rican
                    Government all of the rights both substantive and procedural to which the
                    contract entitles them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
